{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "01", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "00", "M": "53", "S": "25"}}, "news": [{"title": "Nashik civic body's special drive to bring more properties under tax net gets poor response", "para": "Starting September 22, the Nashik Municipal Corporation has kicked off a program aimed at registering unassessed properties. Unfortunately, only 30 property owners have stepped forward in the first week. Municipal Commissioner Manisha Khatri stressed the critical need to boost the municipality's revenue through this effort. With more than six lakh properties documented in Nashik, the NMC is particularly focused on locating unregistered ones before the campaign concludes on October 1.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/nashik-civic-bodys-special-drive-to-bring-more-properties-under-tax-net-gets-poor-response/134579542?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-142866/134579542.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Panchkula: 130  plot owners yet to clear dues under HSVP settlement scheme", "para": "Haryana Shehri Vikas Pradhikaran has outlined 130 Panchkula plots eligible for enhancement charge settlements, providing an extended deadline of December 31. This one-time settlement option is expected to attract numerous beneficiaries, although some local residents express ongoing concerns regarding the enhancement charges. Eligible plot owners can easily check their rebate status and apply through the HSVP website.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/panchkula-130-plot-owners-yet-to-clear-dues-under-hsvp-settlement-scheme/134579472?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-100938/134579472.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Bengaluru's BDA apartments yet to fully turn EV infrastructure switch on", "para": "In Bengaluru, the trend of electric vehicle ownership is gaining momentum in apartment communities. A recent survey indicates that merely one in fifteen BDA complexes boasts a communal charging unit. The majority of residents rely on public charging stations or set up home solutions remotely. Notably, there's a strong enthusiasm among potential buyers for EVs in the coming years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/bengalurus-bda-apartments-yet-to-fully-turn-ev-infrastructure-switch-on/134579407?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-74574/134579407.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}